# Universe Integrity Gate

No new features may be developed until every instrument in `LEGACY_COT_MARKETS` passes the universe integrity audit.

## Required command

```bash
python scripts/run_universe_integrity_audit.py
```

Report: `data/audits/universe_integrity_audit.md`

## Gate rules

- If any instrument fails **identity**, **price**, **COT**, **alignment**, or **derived** validation: **stop**.
- Fix the root cause (do not paper over with aliases or fallback joins).
- Re-run the audit.
- Only proceed with new feature work when the gate is open (`failed == 0`).

## Identity rules

- Canonical join key is HTPL `instrument_id` (e.g. `Gold`, `Japanese Yen / 6J`).
- `cot_market_code` must be the real CFTC contract code — never an OANDA symbol.
- `oanda_symbol` / price provider symbol must be separate from the CFTC code.
- Source of truth: `src/hptl/markets/canonical_identity.py`.

## Do not

- Add fallback mappings or fuzzy aliases to “make the audit pass”
- Join price↔COT on display names or polluted registry fields
- Ship UI/derived work on top of failing instruments
